    "title": "Recurrence expansion",
    "role": "guide",
    "authority": "markdown_source"
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b000001",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 1,
      "end_line": 1,
      "raw": "# Recurrence expansion\n",
      "level": 1,
      "title": "Recurrence expansion"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000002",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 2,
      "end_line": 2,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000003",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 3,
      "end_line": 7,
      "raw": "Expansion reuses the current calendar month's length when evaluating negative\nmonth days or ordinal weekdays. Calendar month arithmetic and epoch conversion\nrun once per encountered year/month/leap-month combination rather than once per\ncandidate day. The cache belongs to one expansion call and uses the selected\n`CalendarSystem`; it does not assume Gregorian month lengths.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000004",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 8,
      "end_line": 8,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 9,
      "end_line": 13,
      "raw": "The recurrence scan still counts every scanned day, preserving scan limits,\nCOUNT, exclusions, additional dates, DST handling and overlap behavior. The\ntests compare a custom counting calendar with Gregorian results across a leap\nyear, verify month-arithmetic call bounds and retain the existing non-Gregorian,\nordinal weekday, ambiguous-time and occurrence-limit cases.\n"
    }
  ],
